# Configuration for `act` (runs the GitHub Actions workflow locally in Docker).
# Kept in the repo so ./dev act works the same for everyone.

# Pin the runner image, otherwise act drops into an interactive picker and
# dies on EOF when run non-interactively. "Medium" is act's own recommended
# default: ~500MB, carries the tooling most actions expect.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# Do not force-pull images. With Docker Desktop's "desktop" credsStore and no
# Docker Hub login, act asks the credential helper for docker.io, gets nothing
# usable, and sends it anyway -- the pull then fails with "authentication
# required" even though the same image pulls fine anonymously. Using the local
# image avoids that path. Refresh images by hand with `docker pull` when needed.
--pull=false
